# RHD Bearings - Model Generation Rules
# Critical compliance requirements extracted from bearing_model_generation_instructions.md
# This file ensures token-efficient access to mandatory rules for automated generation

## ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN - WILL CAUSE IMMEDIATE FAILURE

### Data Generation Violations
- **NEVER generate clearance, vibration, noise, SKF, or material data** - use lookup tables ONLY
- **NEVER estimate or assume technical specifications** - use actual data or null values
- **NEVER hallucinate specifications** when data is not found in lookup tables

### Application Group Violations
- **NEVER group bearings by bore diameter ranges** (5-10mm, 10-20mm, etc.)
- **NEVER copy identical application lists** (4+ matching items) from any bearing model
- **NEVER use identical application group titles** across different bearing models
- **NEVER rotate/rearrange the same application blocks** between bearing models
- **NEVER use generic titles** like "Industrial", "Automotive", "Consumer", "Versatile Solutions", "Precision Instruments"

### Structure Violations
- **NEVER add, delete, or rename JSON fields**
- **NEVER change field types or nested structure**
- **NEVER modify bearing_template.json structure**

## MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS - MUST BE COMPLETED

### Data Source Requirements
- **SKF dimensions**: Look up exact model in skf_dimensions_only.json - if NOT found, set ALL SKF fields to null (never generate or estimate)
- **Vibration data**: Look up bore diameter in vibration_lookup_table.json
- **Noise data**: Look up bore diameter + series in noise_lookup_table.json
- **Clearance data**: Use range logic in clearance_lookup_table.json (over_mm < bore ≤ to_mm)
- **Enhanced description**: Look up exact model in witty_bearing_descriptions.json
- **Base specs**: Extract from bearing_database.json by exact model match

### Application Group Requirements
- **Individual analysis**: Each bearing analyzed based on complete d×D×B×Cr×Cor×RPM×weight profile
- **Model-specific applications**: Generate applications that reflect THIS bearing's specific capabilities
- **Limited overlap allowed**: Individual applications may repeat when technically appropriate
- **List copying prohibited**: Application lists with 4+ identical items are forbidden regardless of position
- **Title uniqueness required**: Application group titles must be model-specific, not generic across models
- **Specification references required**: Requirements text must reference actual bearing specifications
- **Icon assignment**: Select appropriate icon from approved list matching application theme

### Cross-References Requirements
- **Related models**: Up to 4 models sharing same bore size
  - Miniature series: Last digit = bore size (604 relates to 624, 634, 684, 694)
  - Standard series: Last 2 digits × 5 = bore size (6004 relates to 6204, 6304, 6804, 6904)
- **Shaft requirements**: Dynamic h6 calculation based on bore diameter with universal surface finish and runout values
- **Application alternatives**: Use hardcoded values (C3 clearance, RHD V3/V4, SS bearings)

### Content Count Requirements
- **Application groups**: Exactly 3 per bearing model
- **Applications per group**: Exactly 8 relevant items
- **FAQ questions**: Exactly 12 total (3 per category)
- **Recommendation snippets**: Exactly 6 items (15-25 words each)
- **Natural language queries**: Exactly 6 items (5-15 words each)
- **Decision criteria**: Exactly 5 items (10-20 words each)
- **SEO keywords**: 15-25 items

## CRITICAL VALIDATION CHECKPOINTS

### Pre-Generation Validation
- [ ] I have access to all required lookup table files
- [ ] I understand missing data requires null values, never estimation
- [ ] I will analyze each bearing individually based on complete specifications
- [ ] I will not copy entire application group blocks

### Data Accuracy Validation
- [ ] All technical data sourced from lookup tables or set to null
- [ ] All lookup attempts documented (found/not found status)
- [ ] SKF dimensions either exact values or null (never zero)
- [ ] No generated, estimated, or assumed values used

### Application Quality Validation
- [ ] Applications technically appropriate for bearing specifications
- [ ] No copying of identical application lists (4+ matching items) between models
- [ ] Application group titles are model-specific, not generic or repeated across models
- [ ] No systematic rotation of same application blocks between models
- [ ] Individual applications may overlap when technically justified (1-3 items maximum)
- [ ] Requirements text references actual bearing specifications (bore, load, speed)
- [ ] Icons match application group themes per selection rules

### Structure and Content Validation
- [ ] JSON structure matches bearing_template.json exactly
- [ ] All content counts meet exact requirements
- [ ] Cross-references include related models and shaft requirements
- [ ] Application alternatives use hardcoded standardized text

## ICON SELECTION RULES

Choose icons matching application themes:
- **cog**: Mechanical systems, precision instruments, machinery
- **zap**: High-speed applications, electronic devices, power transmission
- **target**: Precision applications, measurement devices, calibration
- **layers**: Multi-component assemblies, stacked systems, complex mechanisms
- **settings**: Automated systems, control devices, adjustment mechanisms
- **cpu**: Electronic components, computing devices, digital systems
- **compass**: Navigation equipment, positioning systems, directional controls
- **gauge**: Measurement instruments, monitoring devices, sensor applications

## SHAFT REQUIREMENTS CALCULATION

Generate dynamically based on bearing's bore diameter:
- **nominal_diameter**: Bore diameter with .000mm precision (e.g., "8.000mm")
- **tolerance_grade**: h6 calculation using ISO ranges (3-6mm: -0.008/0mm, 6-10mm: -0.009/0mm, etc.)
- **surface_finish**: "Ra 0.8μm max" (universal)
- **runout_tolerance**: "0.013mm max" (universal)

## APPLICATION-SPECIFIC ALTERNATIVES (HARDCODED)

Use exact text for ALL bearing models:
```json
"application_specific_alternatives": {
  "high_temperature": "C3 clearance recommended",
  "high_speed": "RHD V3 & V4 bearings recommended", 
  "corrosive_environment": "SS (Stainless Steel) bearings recommended"
}
```

## IMMEDIATE FAILURE TRIGGERS

Stop generation immediately if:
- **Technical data estimated or assumed** instead of looked up
- **SKF dimensions generated** when data exists in lookup tables
- **Placeholder values used** instead of null for missing data
- **Identical application lists copied** (4+ matching items) between bearing models
- **Identical application group titles used** across different bearing models
- **Systematic rotation of application blocks** detected between models
- **Generic application titles** used (Industrial, Automotive, Versatile, Precision Instruments, etc.)
- **Bore range categorization** logic detected

## SUCCESS PATTERN

1. **Verify lookup table access** before starting
2. **Extract base specifications** from bearing_database.json
3. **Perform all data lookups** with proper null handling
4. **Analyze complete bearing profile** individually
5. **Generate technically appropriate applications** based on specifications
6. **Calculate cross-references and shaft requirements** using defined logic
7. **Validate structure and content** before saving

---

**REMEMBER**: Use lookup tables for all technical data. Allow natural application overlap. Prevent wholesale block copying. Focus on technical appropriateness over artificial uniqueness.